<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aghsartan II of Kakheti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">early 12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aghsartan II was the last king of Kakheti and Hereti in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a>. In 1104 nobles of Hereti seized him and handed him over to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">King David</a> IV the Builder, who annexed his kingdom to the Kingdom of Georgia, a major step in David's unification of the country.</p></div>
